* **Example:** If you want to buy a $350,000 home and put down 20% to avoid Private Mortgage Insurance (PMI), you will need $70,000. 
* **Timeline:** To save $70,000 in 24 months, you would need to save about $2,916 per month. 
* *Note:* You can also buy a home with a smaller down payment (e.g., 3% to 5% for conventional loans, or 3.5% for FHA), which would drastically reduce your monthly savings target, though your monthly mortgage payments will be higher.

### 2. Evaluate Your Auto Loan
You have a $19,500 balance on your auto loan with Discover. Check the interest rate on this loan:
* **High Interest (Above 6-7%):** You may want to allocate some extra funds to pay this down faster. High-interest debt eats into your ability to build wealth.
* **Low Interest (Below 5%):** It makes more sense to make the minimum payments and funnel your extra cash into your down payment savings, as your savings can earn a comparable or better yield.

### 3. Protect Your Emergency Fund
You currently have $9,200 in savings. 
* Ideally, you should keep 3 to 6 months' worth of essential living expenses in a separate emergency fund. 
* If your monthly expenses (rent, food, utilities, car payment, insurance) total around $3,500, your $9,200 covers about 2.5 months. You might want to bump this up to $10,000–$15,000 and leave it untouched so your down payment fund isn't derailed by an unexpected expense.

