You currently have $9,200 in savings. Since your timeline is exactly two years, you should avoid putting your down payment funds into the stock market, as it is too volatile for short-term goals. 
*   **Action:** Make sure your savings are in a **High-Yield Savings Account (HYSA)** or a Certificate of Deposit (CD). If your savings are currently sitting in a standard TD Bank account earning little to no interest, moving them to an HYSA earning 4-5% APY will give you free money over the next 24 months.

### 3. Evaluate Your Auto Loan
You have $19,500 left on your Discover auto loan. Check the interest rate on this loan:
*   **If the rate is low (under 5%):** Just continue making your minimum monthly payments and focus all your extra cash on saving for the down payment.
