You currently have $9,200 in savings. Before allocating this to a house, ensure you have a dedicated **Emergency Fund** covering 3 to 6 months of essential living expenses. If your basic expenses (rent, car payment, groceries, utilities) are around $3,500/month, you should ideally keep $10,000+ untouched for emergencies. You may need to build this up slightly before pivoting entirely to the house fund.

